cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the routing benchmark, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "PrismPath: agent workflows as data"
authors:
  - name: "Crystal Warden Labs"
version: 0.1.0
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/OWNER/prismpath"
abstract: >-
  A workflow format and reference implementation in which the control flow of LLM-agent
  systems is a human-authored Markdown document: a routing spectrum of four edge tiers
  (deterministic predicates, embedding-with-LLM-escalation semantics, error, event), a
  decidable static-analysis pass, a routing lockfile, risk-controlled escalation calibration,
  durable execution with a git proof-ledger, a machine-checkable conformance-vector suite,
  and a dependency-free portable kernel for the ML-free subset.
keywords:
  - llm-agents
  - workflow-orchestration
  - markdown
  - routing
  - declarative
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: "A Routing Spectrum for Human-Authored LLM-Agent Workflows: When Control Flow Is Data, Not Code"
  authors:
    - name: "Crystal Warden Labs"
  year: 2026
  notes: "Preprint in docs/papers/; arXiv identifier to be added on submission."
